GIMP Palette
Name: paper-theatre - example (bright matinee, a fairy-tale forest)
Columns: 5
# One instance of the colour structure in style.md (demo.html's "Matinee" scheme). Never ship it
# as is: every game re-chooses each role, and its lighting, for its own tone. The demo's "Night"
# scheme fills the same roles and passes the same rules.
# Checked with the colour-rules (value = HSV V, chroma = S x V, contrast = WCAG ratio):
#   ink on paper 13.13:1; ink on every tint, backdrop and depth role >= 3.69:1 (lowest tint-cloth)
#   paper on card 8.11:1; every backdrop, depth row and the boards separate from paper or card >= 3.25:1
#   depth rows against backdrop-sky: far 1.15 < mid 1.54 < near 2.56
#   chroma of tints, backdrop, depth and proscenium <= 0.49 (ceiling 0.55); accent chroma 0.78
#   accent hue >= 65 deg from every coloured tint and signal; signals on paper >= 5.24:1, chroma >= 0.30
#   proscenium on house 2.63:1; light-key value 1.00
